            <div xml:id="d915">

                <pb facs="0834" n="718" xml:id="pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2746.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following telegram, dated El Paso, Texas, February 6, 1912, from Colonel Edgar Z.
                    Steever, Fourth Cavalry, commanding Fort Bliss, Texas, repeated for your
                    information: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Thirteen mounted and armed Mexicans invaded United States territory at
                            Noria, New Mexico, thirty miles west of El Paso today. Immediately sent
                            detachment by train which captured the whole outfit and sixteen horses.
                            Prisoners now in guard house. Railroad officials afraid the Mexicans
                            intended to hold up express trains; Noria only two miles north of
                            international boundary. Juárez continues tranquil.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. L. Stimson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
